<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gongsun Yuan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 238</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gongsun Yuan was the last ruler of the Gongsun family's regime in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a>, in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. He seized power in 228, courted Eastern Wu and then killed its envoys to please <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-wei">Cao Wei</a>, and in 237 proclaimed himself King of Yan. In 238 Cao Wei sent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sima-yi">Sima Yi</a>, who besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaoyang">Xiangping</a> and killed him.</p></div>
